# nr-tui-mouse: wire lines for mixdog-tui (mouse gestures, wheel routing, edge autoscroll, selection focus/geometry/paint/stitch, copy)

## native/core/Cargo.toml, native/core/Cargo.lock, mixdog-workspace-hack

None. The crate is already a workspace member and takes no new dependency edge: the code uses `mixdog-term` (`MouseReport`,
`selection::{SelectionRect, PaintQueue, clip_selection_rect, word_rect_at ...}`, `modes::ModeEnv`), `mixdog-js`
(`js_trim`, `js_trim_end`, `string_to_number`) and the crate's own `slash::commands::OverlayOwner` and `transcript::*`.

## compose_flip.rs / protocol

None: nothing here is served, no protocol method, no SERVICE_PENDING entry.

## What the application (the run loop, `nr-tui-handlers`, `nr-tui-repl`, `nr-tui-view`) applies

* One `mixdog_tui::mouse::Mouse::new(MouseConfig::from_env(STATUSLINE_BAND_ROWS))` per session. After every layout it calls
  `set_frame(rows, columns)`, `set_transcript_viewport(top, bottom)`, `set_prompt_box_rect(..)` and, when the theme changes,
  `set_selection_background(mixdog_term::selection::selection_background(theme.selectionHighlightBackground || theme.selectionBackground))`.
* The application implements `mouse::MouseHost` (over the render selection of `mixdog_term::selection::SelectionState`, the
  prompt editor's `mouse_*` methods as `mouse::PromptSelection`, the scroll engine, the slash palette, the clipboard through
  `mixdog_term::clipboard::copy_to_clipboard(out, text, false)`, and the hint band). `queue_scroll_coalesced` and
  `scroll_transcript_rows` scroll through `TranscriptScroll::scroll_rows(&mut mouse::scroll::SelectionScroll { mouse, store, inner, now_ms }, ..)`
  so the selection follows the content; `passthrough_ctrl_wheel_zoom` writes what
  `mixdog_term::modes::MouseTrackingRestore::passthrough(now)` returns and the restore it schedules; `force_render_repaint` is
  `PacedFrames`'s `force_full_repaint`.
* Every decoded `InputEvent` mouse report goes to `Mouse::handle_report(&report, host, now_ms)` (wheel reports included: the
  wheel router reads `report.ctrl`). Any keystroke first calls `Mouse::settle_stuck_drag`. Ctrl+C with a live selection calls
  `Mouse::copy_selection(host, 0, now_ms)` and swallows the key. Shift+Arrow/Home/End on a live grid selection (gated by
  `Mouse::grid_selection_active()`) call `Mouse::move_selection_focus(host, FocusMove::.., now_ms)`.
* The loop's timers: it wakes at `Mouse::next_deadline()` (the trailing motion paint, the 50 ms edge autoscroll, the copy retry) and
  calls `Mouse::tick(host, now_ms)`; it also ticks the wheel coalescer (`ScrollCoalescer::deadline`). After every painted frame it
  calls `Mouse::after_frame(store)` (the text capture and stitch harvest that Node ran after the renderer's acknowledgement).

## Notes for the lead

* Twin: `tests/mouse.rs` replays `tests/goldens/mouse.json`; recorded with
  `node native/core/crates/mixdog-tui/tests/recorders/record-mouse.mjs --tree C:/Project/mixdog --write native/core/crates/mixdog-tui/tests/goldens/mouse.json`
  and checked with `--check` (same command). The recorder replaces `clipboard.mjs` for the copy hook with a recording stub through a
  module loader hook (it never touches the clipboard) and drives the hooks on a fake clock.
* Not compiled here (cargo was not run): the crate and its tests are written against the signatures read in `mixdog-term`
  (`selection.rs`, `input/mouse.rs`, `modes.rs`) and `transcript::scroll::engine`.
